      "text": "Manuel Antonio National Park"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c3048f92b8c589363e19aab07c454d5ff0829097d93195a59942e4ab5356eb42",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-63081f33d4c840e99362579a12d8b39a",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on a guided visit to Manuel Antonio National Park, where tropical forest meets the beach. As you walk, you may spot monkeys, sloths, birds, reptiles and butterflies. Your guide will help you find animals among the leaves and explain how the local ecosystem works.\n\nThe trail leads to one of the park’s beaches, which Forbes has named among the world’s most beautiful. You’ll stop by the water for about 20 minutes, with dense tropical forest on one side and white sand and the blue Pacific on the other. After the break, continue through the park.\n\nBreakfast and lunch are included."
    },
